2. Auto-Login Script

Add this at the very bottom of the <script> section (just before the closing </script> tag):

```javascript
// ===== AUTO-LOGIN - BYPASS LOGIN SCREEN =====
(function() {
    // Set as admin with full permissions
    currentUser.role = 'admin';
    currentUser.name = 'System Administrator';
    currentUser.permissions = ['all'];
    
    // Update UI
    const badge = document.getElementById('currentUserRole');
    if (badge) {
        badge.textContent = 'System Administrator';
        badge.className = 'badge bg-danger text-dark mt-1';
    }
    
    // Hide login screen
    const loginScreen = document.getElementById('login-screen');
    if (loginScreen) {
        loginScreen.style.display = 'none';
    }
    
    // Log the login
    auditLog.log('USER_AUTO_LOGIN', { role: 'admin' });
    
    console.log('✅ Auto-logged in as System Administrator (Full Access)');
})();
```

---

That's It!

Just these 2 changes and the app will:

· ✅ Load straight to the dashboard
· ✅ Have full admin permissions (create, edit, delete everything)
· ✅ Show "System Administrator" as the role
· ✅ Keep the login screen completely hidden (but still in the code if you ever want to restore it)

Total changes: 2 edits
Time to implement: ~30 seconds

The login screen is just commented out, so you can easily restore it later by uncommenting the HTML and removing the auto-login script.
